# PathTrackingReport: generated by tools/generate_interfaces.py from more_generic_models 0.1.0. Do not edit.
# The guidance's track of the leg the vehicle follows, from the previous period's ``TrackState`` (the estimate's, never the
# truth's): ``leg_start`` and ``leg_end`` the two waypoints of the leg as (north, east, z) in NED metres about the scenario
# origin, z in the unit of the route (NaN triples: an orbit, or no leg); ``along_track`` and ``cross_track`` (m, in the leg's
# frame, cross-track positive to starboard of the leg), ``vertical_track`` (m, depth minus the depth reference), ``course_error``
# (rad, course over ground minus the leg's bearing, wrapped to (-pi, pi]), ``time_to_go`` (s: the distance left on the leg, leg
# length minus along-track, over the leg's commanded speed; 0 when finished, NaN with no speed) and ``near_end`` (the vehicle is
# inside the leg's end radius). Issued only while a route is followed.
#
# Frames (owner decision): positions NED about the scenario origin (x north, y east), body quantities FRD, angles in rad from
# north clockwise, time in s on the scenario clock.
std_msgs/Header header  # stamp = t rounded to ns; frame_id map_ned for positions
uint64 stream_seq  # publication counter per vehicle across all report types (restores the drain order)
float64 t  # unit: s; the sample instant on the scenario clock, exactly
float64[3] leg_start  # components in order: north, east, z; unit: mixed; frame: ned; (north m, east m, z m): z in the unit named by ``z_mode``
float64[3] leg_end  # components in order: north, east, z; unit: mixed; frame: ned; (north m, east m, z m): z in the unit named by ``z_mode``
float64 along_track  # unit: m; frame: leg
float64 cross_track  # unit: m; frame: leg
float64 vertical_track  # unit: m; frame: depth_down
float64 course_error  # unit: rad; frame: ned
float64 time_to_go  # unit: s
bool near_end  # unit: flag
string z_mode "none"  # unit: enum; the vertical reference of the z of ``leg_start`` and ``leg_end`` (the unit is m): the route's ``z_mode``; ``none`` when no route is known
